From 6e4290ec0cb9c4953049a1157b423c5a4217c427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 17:05:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen the type-feedback census past the seven suites it could
 reach
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Item 2-13 established that this engine's largest private deficiency is zlib —
12.0x behind Jint relative to Chromium — so the next step was to ask what the
censuses say about it. They say nothing: zlib is in none of them, and neither
are Mandreel, Gameboy, PdfJS, Typescript, CodeLoad, Splay or RegExp.

TypeFeedbackMetrics, SpecializingTierMetrics and PropertyMapDistributionMetrics
all ran the same seven suites, and the roadmap quotes their output as "the
corpus" — the phrase every phase-3 and phase-4 headline uses, over a denominator
that was never stated.

Why it was seven had not been written down, and is not a choice about cost.
Widening the list and running it aborts at the ninth suite with an uncatchable
.NET stack overflow in Mandreel's global_init. Item 0-2's 16 MiB thread and
4 MiB reserve are a property of Broiler.JavaScript/Program.cs — the shell — and
BenchmarkContext.Create built a plain JSContext on whatever stack the runtime
handed Main. Every benchmark host in this campaign has been running without the
reserve the shell has had since phase 0.

The census also serialized its report once, at the end, so that abort discarded
the eight suites that had already run — a partial corpus that cannot produce a
partial result.

Both fixed. The census runs on the shell's thread with the shell's
MaxStackUsageBytes, and writes after every suite. Mandreel now fails the way the
shell makes it fail, catchably, instead of taking the process down. The corpus
aggregate is emitted by the instrument with its suite count beside it, rather
than left to be totalled by whoever quotes it.

The widened count moves phase 4's premise. The old seven reproduce to the digit
— 93.54% of 37.9 M reads, 96.70% of 4.24 M calls — so this is the same
instrument over a bigger corpus. Every suite that runs: 80.11% of 307.9 M reads
and 86.35% of 52.9 M calls, with 87.7% of the reads outside the seven. The two
suites that move it had never been counted: Gameboy at 34.60% monomorphic with
1 282 polymorphic sites, and Splay at 10.15%.

Three suites still report setup-only counts — zlib needs the shell's `read`
builtin, Mandreel now hits the guard, RegExp has its pre-existing checksum
defect — together 0.09% of reads, so the headline is over 12 suites and says so.

